      "summary": "The system under test runs on IBM Code Engine and the k6 load generator runs from a separate client machine. This reduces the same-host interference present in the earlier development-host dataset, although public-network variability and managed-platform behavior can still affect latency measurements.",
      "ta_feedback": "Good progress so far, and it\u2019s great to see clear experiments with meaningful results showing how the system behaves under increasing load. The current tests simulate virtual users sending requests through the system, but since both the load generator and all services are running on the same machine, they may interfere with each other and affect the accuracy of the results. This setup can make it harder to clearly identify real bottlenecks or reflect realistic system behavior. For the final report, try to separate the load generation from the system or clearly explain how this limitation may impact your findings."
    }
